-# UX round 3 (A2) / round 4 (R4-3) — the Resettlement Case facts in the About info grid,
-# as an item-appender (renders nothing; mutates the caller's items array). Only the facts
-# the About grid does NOT already carry: case state, intake date, the CASE household (can
-# differ from the non-case families item), and the exit date for a closed case. Case
-# Manager / Status stay in their canonical spots (case-worker item / header badge);
-# Edit/Exit live in the header Actions dropdown.
-# locals: client:, items:
- current_case = client.cases.exclude_referred.current
- if current_case.present?
  - items << info_item(t('clients.show.resettlement_case', default: 'Case'), t('clients.show.case_active', default: 'Active'))
  - items << info_item(t('clients.show.intake_date', default: 'Intake date'), (date_format(current_case.start_date) if current_case.start_date))
  -# (Pre-production polish: the "Case household" item is gone — the About grid's single
  -# Household row already carries the case's family; two rows read as a confusing dupe.)
- elsif (last_case = client.cases.exclude_referred.inactive.order(:exit_date).last).present?
  - items << info_item(t('clients.show.resettlement_case', default: 'Case'), t('clients.show.case_exited', default: 'Closed'))
  - if last_case.exit_date.present?
    - items << info_item(t('clients.show.case_exit_date', default: 'Case closed on'), date_format(last_case.exit_date))
